Files in this directory whose names end in .properties are loaded on top of
conf/mirth.properties at startup, in lexical filename order. Later files override
earlier ones, and any file here overrides mirth.properties itself.

Put your local customizations here, for example:

    10-database.properties
    20-ports.properties

The server never writes to this directory, unlike mirth.properties, which it
rewrites during version migration and password encryption. That also means
properties the server encrypts and writes back (database.password,
database-readonly.password, keystore.storepass, keystore.keypass) should stay in
mirth.properties: if you override one of them here, your plaintext value keeps
taking precedence and will not be encrypted.

Files are parsed with java.util.Properties semantics. If a key appears more than
once, the last occurrence wins; there are no multi-valued properties. For list
properties such as https.client.protocols, use a single comma-separated value.
